      "writtenOn": "2026-10-07T10:33:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PDI default for PowerCap is maxint (\"not set\"), and 86196 maps maxint to SetPoint null. Initialising to 0 reports a 0 W cap until the first successful read. Should this be std::numeric_limits\u003cuint32_t\u003e::max()?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "ee3c850dbb702e55156378dd970dbb421a179f45",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01ffb378_f87a66e8",
        "filename": "platform-mc/effecters/numeric/power_cap_dbus_intf.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002771
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-07T10:33:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reading comes from the device and goes through rawToBase(), so a signed effecter size or a negative offset can give a negative value, and a resolution \u003e 1 can exceed UINT32_MAX. Casting such a value to uint32 is undefined behaviour. Suggest skipping the update with an error log when the value is outside [0, UINT32_MAX].",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "ee3c850dbb702e55156378dd970dbb421a179f45",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
